    "eng_translation": [
      "fulvestrant",
      "Fulvestrant is a selective estrogen receptor downregulator (SERD) used in the treatment of hormone receptor-positive breast cancer in postmenopausal women. It works by binding to and inactivating estrogen receptors, thereby inhibiting the growth of breast cancer cells that depend on estrogen for proliferation. Fulvestrant is typically used in patients who have developed resistance to other endocrine therapies, such as aromatase inhibitors or tamoxifen. It is administered as a subcutaneous injection and is associated with a range of side effects, including hot flashes, fatigue, and musculoskeletal pain. The drug is approved for use in both early and advanced stages of breast cancer, depending on the patient's specific clinical situation."
